                    text: "Done. The recorder is now installed at `~/.cargo/bin/agent_session_recorder` and Zed points at it instead of the debug build in `target/`.\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **Doc comment** in `crates/agent_session/examples/agent_session_recorder.rs` — the build command is now `cargo install --locked --path crates/agent_session --example agent_session_recorder`, and the sample Zed config uses `\"$HOME/.cargo/bin/agent_session_recorder\"` (bash expands `$HOME`, so no hardcoded repo path).\n2. **`~/.config/zed/settings.json`** — the \"Recorded Claude\" agent server now execs the installed binary via `$HOME/.cargo/bin` instead of `/Users/eric/Code/macro/target/debug/examples/...`.\n3. **Ran the install** — it succeeded and the binary is in place. One wrinkle worth knowing: plain `cargo install` failed because it ignores `Cargo.lock` and resolved an `aws-types` that needs rustc 1.94.1 (the repo pins 1.94.0). `--locked` fixes that, which is why it's in the documented command.\n\nAfter future changes to the recorder, re-run the install command to refresh the binary — Zed no longer picks up `cargo build` output automatically.Yes — in your user-level Zed settings at `~/.config/zed/settings.json` (the `agent_servers` block wasn't in the project's `.zed/settings.json`). The \"Recorded Claude\" entry's command changed from:\n\n```\nexec env -u ANTHROPIC_API_KEY /Users/eric/Code/macro/target/debug/examples/agent_session_recorder\n```\n\nto:\n\n```\nexec env -u ANTHROPIC_API_KEY \"$HOME/.cargo/bin/agent_session_recorder\"\n```\n\nEverything else in the file is untouched. You may need to restart the agent server in Zed (or reopen the panel) for it to pick up the new command.",
